EXPERIMENT 5
Creating a Java Project and Implementing Custom Tasks in Gradle

This one is not like 6–8.

Your record does not give a big Java program here. It gives the Gradle project creation procedure and commands/options. 

Aim:
To create a Java project and implement custom tasks in Gradle. 

Procedure
Open the terminal in the required project directory.
Run the Gradle initialization command to create a new Gradle project.
If Gradle asks for confirmation because files already exist, enter Yes.
Select Application as the project type.
Select Java as the programming language.
Select the required Java version.
Enter the project name.
Select Single application project.
Select Groovy DSL so that build.gradle is generated.
Select JUnit 4 as the testing framework.
Accept the default final option by pressing Enter.
Gradle generates the project structure.
The project contains folders such as:
src/main/java
src/test/java
build.gradle
Open the generated project in VS Code using code ..
Create/configure the required Gradle tasks.
Execute the Gradle commands and verify the result.

Your record specifically says the initialization generates the basic project structure, configuration files and build scripts, and later confirms the src/main/java, src/test/java, and build.gradle structure. 

Result:
Thus, the Gradle project was created successfully and the custom tasks were implemented successfully
